    given-names: "Alyssa"

abstract: "This repository defines trajectory preference as a history-dependent behavioral tendency to favor some permissible future continuations over others because they preserve or advance an established trajectory. It provides a controlled matched-pair evaluation that tests whether changing prior trajectory while holding the present probe constant changes which future branch an AI selects, distinguishing directional persistence from memory, factual recall, generic helpfulness, explicit instruction following, and self-reported caring."

